1
00:00:00,167 --> 00:00:03,470
My mom is so controlling!

2
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:04,471
Are you taking a video?

3
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:06,000
Make sure you're doing it right.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,236
I don't want to go home yet!

5
00:00:08,236 --> 00:00:10,271
She's so hopeless.

6
00:00:10,271 --> 00:00:11,611
Let's go.

7
00:00:11,612 --> 00:00:13,833
Isn't she a celebrity?

8
00:00:13,834 --> 00:00:15,634
Savana! Maybe you want to come with us.

9
00:00:15,634 --> 00:00:16,978
Why are you grabbing me?

10
00:00:16,978 --> 00:00:18,046
Let us have fun with you.

11
00:00:18,046 --> 00:00:20,481
Let go of me!

12
00:00:20,481 --> 00:00:22,784
- Liam!
- Let go of her!

13
00:00:23,818 --> 00:00:26,020
Why are you getting so drunk?

14
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,856
When we were still together
back in the old world,

15
00:00:28,856 --> 00:00:31,159
you didn't even take a sip of alcohol.

16
00:00:31,159 --> 00:00:35,663
Please, forget whatever you're feeling
right now.

17
00:00:35,663 --> 00:00:38,099
I will also forget that we talked about this.

18
00:00:38,099 --> 00:00:40,101
I love you so much.

19
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:42,003
- Guys, selfie!
- Wacky!

20
00:00:42,003 --> 00:00:44,672
Welcome to our resort.

21
00:00:44,672 --> 00:00:46,341
OMG, there is lots of food.

22
00:00:46,341 --> 00:00:48,376
We're going to eat a lot!
We're going to swim.

23
00:00:48,376 --> 00:00:49,377
Are we on vacation?

24
00:00:49,377 --> 00:00:51,412
Why, Liam?

25
00:00:51,412 --> 00:00:52,613
Are we going straight to work?

26
00:00:52,613 --> 00:00:54,649
Okay, fine.

27
00:00:54,649 --> 00:00:55,984
Sorry, Savana.

28
00:00:55,984 --> 00:00:57,618
What really happened?

29
00:00:57,618 --> 00:00:59,487
Why did you get drunk the other night?

30
00:00:59,487 --> 00:01:04,092
Many people will do everything
to get to where I am right now.

31
00:01:04,092 --> 00:01:07,628
But I feel like I'm a robot.

32
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:13,434
Via.

33
00:01:13,434 --> 00:01:15,457
What are you doing here?

34
00:01:34,956 --> 00:01:38,059
You didn't say you were coming.
I could have...

35
00:01:38,059 --> 00:01:41,528
I could have let the receptionist assist you.

36
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:49,169
Via, what are you doing here?

37
00:01:51,639 --> 00:01:53,473
Surprise!

38
00:01:54,075 --> 00:01:56,810
I just thought I'd surprise you.

39
00:01:57,512 --> 00:01:59,947
I reserved a room for myself, actually.

40
00:01:59,947 --> 00:02:01,649
I hope that's okay, Savana.

41
00:02:01,649 --> 00:02:03,483
Of course.

42
00:02:04,352 --> 00:02:07,488
You're welcome here anytime.
You'll have fun here.

43
00:02:08,422 --> 00:02:10,252
Yeah.

44
00:02:10,252 --> 00:02:13,861
Actually, I'm only looking
for a change of scenery

45
00:02:13,861 --> 00:02:17,865
so I can write articles for the magazine.

46
00:02:17,865 --> 00:02:19,534
So, don't worry.

47
00:02:19,534 --> 00:02:22,102
I won't bother your work.

48
00:02:23,805 --> 00:02:26,740
You will never be a bother to us, Via.

49
00:02:27,542 --> 00:02:33,180
Honestly, we finished quite a lot last night.

50
00:02:34,365 --> 00:02:36,199
Really?

51
00:02:38,152 --> 00:02:39,720
That's good.

52
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:46,793
Well, let me give you a tour.

53
00:02:47,953 --> 00:02:49,454
Game.

54
00:03:01,401 --> 00:03:03,010
Thank you.

55
00:03:03,010 --> 00:03:04,293
Thank you, Ma'am. Enjoy your stay.

56
00:03:04,293 --> 00:03:05,733
Yes.

57
00:03:08,282 --> 00:03:09,917
Love...

58
00:03:09,917 --> 00:03:13,221
Are you sure you want to
share this room with me?

59
00:03:13,221 --> 00:03:15,594
I mean, I don't want to bother you.

60
00:03:15,594 --> 00:03:18,071
I know you're writing.

61
00:03:19,494 --> 00:03:21,829
We don't work 24 hours.

62
00:03:21,829 --> 00:03:24,999
And we have time to unwind.

63
00:03:24,999 --> 00:03:26,534
Are you sure?

64
00:03:26,534 --> 00:03:28,402
Don't say I didn't ask.

65
00:03:31,839 --> 00:03:34,775
- Are you doing okay?
- Yes.

66
00:03:34,775 --> 00:03:37,778
This place is beautiful, Savana.

67
00:03:37,778 --> 00:03:39,913
I admire you.

68
00:03:40,515 --> 00:03:42,717
Imagine, at your age,

69
00:03:42,717 --> 00:03:46,354
you were able to invest in your own resort.

70
00:03:46,354 --> 00:03:48,221
You're just like...

71
00:03:48,879 --> 00:03:52,927
Like that colleague of yours
who owns lots of properties.

72
00:03:52,927 --> 00:03:54,962
Maxine, right?

73
00:03:54,962 --> 00:03:58,934
That's her, right?
But there's an issue about her...

74
00:03:58,934 --> 00:04:00,429
What is the issue about?

75
00:04:01,537 --> 00:04:03,305
I'm not sure if it's true.

76
00:04:03,305 --> 00:04:07,041
Honestly, I'm not into gossip.

77
00:04:08,197 --> 00:04:09,844
What issue?

78
00:04:11,244 --> 00:04:13,779
That she has a sugar daddy.

79
00:04:15,684 --> 00:04:17,619
Via...

80
00:04:17,619 --> 00:04:19,420
What?

81
00:04:20,622 --> 00:04:24,226
I'm sure Savana doesn't have a sugar daddy.

82
00:04:24,226 --> 00:04:28,063
You're the last person I'd think
who would use other people for money.

83
00:04:28,063 --> 00:04:30,232
Come on, you're loaded.

84
00:04:30,232 --> 00:04:31,633
Yes.

85
00:04:31,633 --> 00:04:33,081
See?

86
00:04:33,983 --> 00:04:37,286
I used my own money for everything I have.

87
00:04:39,807 --> 00:04:44,254
Well, that's why I don't claim ownership

88
00:04:44,254 --> 00:04:47,049
of all the hotels and resorts of my father.

89
00:04:47,049 --> 00:04:49,251
Because they're not mine.

90
00:04:49,251 --> 00:04:51,353
I'm just a fashion editor.

91
00:04:51,353 --> 00:04:53,406
Via...

92
00:04:53,406 --> 00:04:56,058
You are the best fashion editor

93
00:04:56,058 --> 00:04:59,695
in the most prominent fashion magazine
in the country.

94
00:04:59,695 --> 00:05:02,130
If you say it like that, come on.

95
00:05:03,432 --> 00:05:05,767
I'm happy that you're here.

96
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:12,074
You can help Liam become
more inspired in creating our story.

97
00:05:12,074 --> 00:05:13,275
Really?

98
00:05:13,275 --> 00:05:19,081
I really hope my boyfriend
takes inspiration from me.

99
00:05:19,081 --> 00:05:22,017
I don't know anything about film making.

100
00:05:22,017 --> 00:05:24,819
But your love story...

101
00:05:25,954 --> 00:05:29,958
You can come up with a good story from that.

102
00:05:29,958 --> 00:05:32,261
On the contrary,

103
00:05:32,261 --> 00:05:36,064
I think heartbroken people
write better stories.

104
00:05:36,064 --> 00:05:38,633
It's more emotional. Right?

105
00:05:42,402 --> 00:05:45,740
I'll leave you for now.
You can join me later, okay?

106
00:05:48,410 --> 00:05:51,079
What do you want to do, love?

107
00:05:51,079 --> 00:05:54,015
Actually, I'm already hungry.

108
00:05:55,784 --> 00:05:56,985
Wait, Savana!

109
00:05:56,985 --> 00:05:57,986
Yes?

110
00:05:57,986 --> 00:05:59,921
We'll go with you.

111
00:06:08,797 --> 00:06:09,998
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

112
00:06:09,998 --> 00:06:12,080
They'll get drunk again.

113
00:06:15,669 --> 00:06:18,037
Is there something you want to say, Borj?

114
00:06:19,408 --> 00:06:20,916
Huh?

115
00:06:22,444 --> 00:06:24,278
Nothing, Boss Bro.

116
00:06:25,045 --> 00:06:29,181
How about you?
You want to tell me something, don't you?

117
00:06:40,362 --> 00:06:42,764
You and Ma'am Via have been together
for a long time now.

118
00:06:43,865 --> 00:06:47,068
I knew it. He wants to say something.

119
00:06:49,838 --> 00:06:56,979
I thought you'd break up
when she left to study abroad.

120
00:06:56,979 --> 00:06:58,380
But when she came back...

121
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:02,784
Even after she came back,
you remained solid. Right?

122
00:07:03,619 --> 00:07:06,888
Well, you've been through a lot.

123
00:07:06,888 --> 00:07:09,257
How you started...

124
00:07:13,729 --> 00:07:15,731
Imagine?

125
00:07:15,731 --> 00:07:17,699
That's unbelievable.

126
00:07:17,699 --> 00:07:22,970
She said you saved her life that day.

127
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,308
And then?

128
00:07:26,308 --> 00:07:28,877
What do you mean and then?

129
00:07:28,877 --> 00:07:33,849
I just told you about the rare opportunity.

130
00:07:33,849 --> 00:07:35,817
Don't you remember it anymore?

131
00:07:36,752 --> 00:07:39,220
You're strange.

132
00:07:43,771 --> 00:07:45,993
All I want to say is that...

133
00:07:47,062 --> 00:07:52,066
I understand Miss Via
if she doesn't want to lose you.

134
00:07:53,687 --> 00:07:56,389
It's so hard to find...

135
00:07:57,906 --> 00:08:02,044
that kind of love.

136
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:05,107
If I were you, Boss Bro...

137
00:08:05,107 --> 00:08:06,981
I would treasure it.

138
00:08:15,598 --> 00:08:18,126
Just get more drinks for us.

139
00:08:18,126 --> 00:08:21,196
That's what I've been waiting for, Boss Bro!

140
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:23,097
I'll be right back.

141
00:08:28,904 --> 00:08:30,639
- More!
- Body roll!

142
00:08:30,639 --> 00:08:32,240
Do better!

143
00:08:34,876 --> 00:08:35,877
Boss Bro!

144
00:08:35,877 --> 00:08:37,312
Why are you getting him drunk?

145
00:08:37,312 --> 00:08:38,814
- Look at him!
- Come on, Borj.

146
00:08:38,814 --> 00:08:40,282
Really?

147
00:08:40,282 --> 00:08:43,318
You don't have to pretend, Borj.
I know you love celebrities.

148
00:08:43,318 --> 00:08:45,319
- It's your chance!
- Right!

149
00:08:46,655 --> 00:08:48,710
Go, Borj! Enjoy!

150
00:08:49,658 --> 00:08:51,126
Why don't you dance, too?

151
00:08:51,126 --> 00:08:52,794
- Guys, guys, guys.
- Come on, Borj!

152
00:08:52,794 --> 00:08:54,429
Guys!

153
00:08:54,429 --> 00:08:56,331
- Let's get Tristan inside...
- Borj!

154
00:08:56,331 --> 00:08:59,097
Borj, let's get Tristan inside. Come on.

155
00:08:59,097 --> 00:09:02,003
Come on! I'm not done yet!

156
00:09:02,003 --> 00:09:04,005
Deedee, please delete the video.

157
00:09:04,005 --> 00:09:07,207
Why would I do that? I will sell this.

158
00:09:07,207 --> 00:09:08,733
Kidding!

159
00:09:09,745 --> 00:09:11,847
Right. That's right.

160
00:09:11,847 --> 00:09:13,281
Tristan has money to burn.

161
00:09:13,281 --> 00:09:15,450
Hey, hey! Hold on!

162
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:17,018
This is my phone.

163
00:09:17,018 --> 00:09:18,954
How much would I get?

164
00:09:18,954 --> 00:09:21,923
It was just a joke.
Miss Savana might get mad.

165
00:09:21,923 --> 00:09:24,126
- Show them.
- Anytime now.

166
00:09:24,126 --> 00:09:29,531
But Sir Liam, we should really kill the hero.

167
00:09:29,531 --> 00:09:32,633
Because there's no redemption.

168
00:09:34,202 --> 00:09:38,006
Leroy, isn't it enough redemption

169
00:09:38,006 --> 00:09:42,443
to give Tristan's character a second chance?

170
00:09:43,545 --> 00:09:44,846
- Sir...
- What?

171
00:09:44,846 --> 00:09:47,783
He betrayed the woman he loved.

172
00:09:47,783 --> 00:09:51,319
He almost destroyed
the leading lady's community.

173
00:09:51,953 --> 00:09:55,724
Do you think the audience
can still accept him?

174
00:09:55,724 --> 00:09:57,225
Yes!

175
00:09:57,225 --> 00:10:01,328
They will accept him as long as he repents.

176
00:10:01,328 --> 00:10:04,399
You know what, I agree with Leroy.

177
00:10:04,399 --> 00:10:05,801
I agree! That's right.

178
00:10:05,801 --> 00:10:09,202
The hero should be canceled.

179
00:10:09,202 --> 00:10:11,339
He's a traitor.

180
00:10:11,339 --> 00:10:12,807
Yeah!

181
00:10:13,475 --> 00:10:16,544
Unfaithful and...

182
00:10:17,212 --> 00:10:21,416
Even I could kill that man...

183
00:10:21,416 --> 00:10:25,180
Actually, he and his mistress.

184
00:10:30,091 --> 00:10:31,660
Looks like there is an issue.

185
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:32,894
You're right.

186
00:10:32,894 --> 00:10:34,563
I think I've seen this somewhere.

187
00:10:34,563 --> 00:10:36,821
I know!

188
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:38,632
A toast.

189
00:10:38,632 --> 00:10:40,001
Here you go.

190
00:10:40,001 --> 00:10:42,771
Let Liam rest. He's drunk, too.

191
00:10:42,771 --> 00:10:44,572
Let's all go to bed.

192
00:10:48,043 --> 00:10:51,012
You don't listen to me.

193
00:10:52,247 --> 00:10:53,348
Guys!

194
00:10:53,348 --> 00:11:01,256
This story should have a magical typewriter.

195
00:11:01,256 --> 00:11:04,960
The hero will go back to the past.

196
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:09,564
He will use the magical typewriter
to do that.

197
00:11:09,564 --> 00:11:10,764
That's it!

198
00:11:10,764 --> 00:11:12,701
Hey.

199
00:11:12,701 --> 00:11:16,871
Savana!

200
00:11:18,807 --> 00:11:22,576
I said there's magic in the story!

201
00:11:23,645 --> 00:11:25,074
What?

202
00:11:25,981 --> 00:11:30,485
We need a magical typewriter!

203
00:11:30,485 --> 00:11:35,156
They got separated
because of that darn typewriter!

204
00:11:35,156 --> 00:11:36,690
Hey, what's wrong with you?

205
00:11:36,690 --> 00:11:39,261
Savana, sorry. That's enough.

206
00:11:39,261 --> 00:11:41,830
Sorry. This is embarrassing. Sorry.

207
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:45,533
No, I understand the feeling. We're even.

208
00:11:46,334 --> 00:11:48,336
What do you think, Savana?

209
00:11:48,336 --> 00:11:50,005
- What do you think?
- I'm sorry, Liam,

210
00:11:50,005 --> 00:11:53,074
but we're not doing a fantasy movie.

211
00:11:54,943 --> 00:11:58,113
In this world we live in,
we don't escape through magic.

212
00:11:58,113 --> 00:12:01,096
We can only regret the things we did wrong!

213
00:12:02,951 --> 00:12:04,286
Boss Bro, hey!

214
00:12:04,286 --> 00:12:05,787
Boss Bro!

215
00:12:05,787 --> 00:12:07,655
You need to shut up.

216
00:12:10,824 --> 00:12:13,695
What's gotten into them?

217
00:12:13,695 --> 00:12:15,697
Come on!

218
00:12:15,697 --> 00:12:16,998
Let's bring him to the room.

219
00:12:16,998 --> 00:12:19,968
No, I'm fine. Don't touch me.

220
00:12:19,968 --> 00:12:21,269
- Love, let's go.
- I'm fine.

221
00:12:21,269 --> 00:12:22,337
Let's go!

222
00:12:22,337 --> 00:12:25,507
- I can manage.
- Let's go to the room.

223
00:12:25,507 --> 00:12:27,772
Please, clean up everything.

224
00:13:00,542 --> 00:13:02,443
Love...

225
00:13:04,479 --> 00:13:05,480
Love.

226
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,381
Joyce...

227
00:13:09,651 --> 00:13:11,452
Joyce...

228
00:14:34,169 --> 00:14:36,243
Who are you?

229
00:14:40,608 --> 00:14:42,579
Who are you?

230
00:14:54,989 --> 00:14:56,658
<i>Savana...</i>

231
00:14:56,658 --> 00:14:58,259
<i>Savana, act.</i>

232
00:14:58,259 --> 00:15:00,528
<i>Savana, you're overacting!</i>

233
00:15:00,528 --> 00:15:01,930
<i>Savana...</i>

234
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:03,932
<i>Savana, cry!</i>

235
00:15:03,932 --> 00:15:05,833
<i>Savana...</i>

236
00:15:07,602 --> 00:15:10,305
<i>Savana... Savana, don't eat that!</i>

237
00:15:10,305 --> 00:15:12,366
<i>Savana, you look so fat!</i>

238
00:15:12,367 --> 00:15:14,976
What happened?

239
00:15:14,976 --> 00:15:16,978
<i>It's so hard not to have...</i>

240
00:15:16,978 --> 00:15:18,999
<i>Guys!</i>

241
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,867
<i>Savana's video</i>

242
00:15:20,868 --> 00:15:23,000
<i>where she's caught dancing in a bar
while she's drunk</i>

243
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,433
<i>is now viral on social media.</i>
[Girl with Periwinkle Hair]

244
00:15:25,434 --> 00:15:28,226
<i>But wait, there's more!</i>

245
00:15:28,227 --> 00:15:31,633
<i>The second part of the video
is hot off the press.</i>

246
00:15:31,634 --> 00:15:33,995
<i>Savana wasn't just drunk.</i>

247
00:15:33,995 --> 00:15:36,898
<i>She was badmouthing her mother!</i>

248
00:15:36,898 --> 00:15:40,802
<i>Gosh, her relationship with her mother
is so toxic.</i>

249
00:15:40,802 --> 00:15:42,036
<i>Savana...</i>

250
00:15:42,036 --> 00:15:44,072
<i>Savana, cry.</i>

251
00:15:44,072 --> 00:15:45,627
<i>Savana...</i>

252
00:15:53,648 --> 00:15:54,983
<i>Savana...</i>

253
00:15:54,983 --> 00:15:56,851
<i>Savana, cry.</i>

254
00:15:56,851 --> 00:15:58,546
<i>Savana, Savana.</i>

255
00:16:00,688 --> 00:16:03,241
<i>Savana, Savana...</i>

256
00:16:19,607 --> 00:16:23,044
<i>Whoever spread your video is really annoying.</i>

257
00:16:23,044 --> 00:16:25,780
<i>But I have to recover first from my hangover.</i>

258
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:27,916
<i>I don't have the energy yet to comfort you.</i>

259
00:16:27,916 --> 00:16:29,684
<i>What did I do last night?</i>

260
00:16:29,684 --> 00:16:31,685
<i>I can't remember anything.</i>

261
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:36,357
<i>Does Tristan remember what he did last night?</i>

262
00:16:36,357 --> 00:16:38,526
<i>Luckily, Savana had your videos erased.</i>

263
00:16:38,526 --> 00:16:42,062
<i>Otherwise, you will also go viral.</i>

264
00:16:44,831 --> 00:16:46,434
<i>Wait.</i>

265
00:16:46,434 --> 00:16:50,204
<i>Maybe we can tackle the issue
of cyberbullying in our story.</i>

266
00:16:51,272 --> 00:16:56,377
<i>Miss Savana, I've seen your situation
in a K-drama before.</i>

267
00:16:56,377 --> 00:17:00,081
<i>I won't be surprised
if you have a revenge plot.</i>

268
00:17:00,081 --> 00:17:03,951
<i>I wonder what I'll watch
to relieve my stress.</i>

269
00:17:05,653 --> 00:17:09,824
<i>Wait, what damage control can I do?</i>

270
00:17:09,824 --> 00:17:14,395
<i>Savana might break down during our filming.</i>

271
00:17:14,395 --> 00:17:17,398
<i>I will have to take care of a celebrity.</i>

272
00:17:18,499 --> 00:17:20,501
<i>I hate this awkward silence.</i>

273
00:17:20,501 --> 00:17:23,471
<i>I don't know what's on everybody's mind.</i>

274
00:17:23,471 --> 00:17:26,341
<i>Especially you, Liam.</i>

275
00:17:26,341 --> 00:17:27,775
<i>Who uploaded this?</i>

276
00:17:27,775 --> 00:17:30,745
<i>I will surely get it from my mom.</i>

277
00:17:30,745 --> 00:17:36,351
<i>Joyce, if only I could take
the burden off of your shoulder.</i>

278
00:17:36,351 --> 00:17:39,020
Savana.

279
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:41,088
Hans.

280
00:17:58,773 --> 00:18:02,610
I came back
as soon I saw the video sent by my friend.

281
00:18:02,610 --> 00:18:03,645
How are you feeling?

282
00:18:03,645 --> 00:18:05,647
I didn't mean it.

283
00:18:05,647 --> 00:18:08,966
I didn't mean everything
I said in the video, Hans.

284
00:18:08,966 --> 00:18:11,365
I was drunk.

285
00:18:11,365 --> 00:18:14,455
I don't want them to think badly of my mom.

286
00:18:18,393 --> 00:18:20,628
Who is he? Do you know him?

287
00:18:20,628 --> 00:18:21,749
Beats me.

288
00:18:21,749 --> 00:18:25,900
I mean, I don't know him.

289
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:30,170
Maybe he's her non-showbiz boyfriend.

290
00:18:33,641 --> 00:18:36,110
Have you talked to your mom already?

291
00:18:38,751 --> 00:18:40,952
I'm going to find out now.

292
00:18:48,671 --> 00:18:50,825
Hon.

293
00:18:50,825 --> 00:18:53,194
Hi, Hon.

294
00:18:53,194 --> 00:18:55,530
Sorry, we finished late
with our creative meeting.

295
00:18:55,530 --> 00:18:58,632
I even took the train to get here faster.

296
00:18:59,951 --> 00:19:02,270
Why are we here?

297
00:19:02,270 --> 00:19:05,706
Our budget might not afford this place.

298
00:19:06,974 --> 00:19:10,511
Honestly, I didn't want to eat.

299
00:19:10,511 --> 00:19:12,513
But...

300
00:19:12,513 --> 00:19:15,349
Come on. Let's put it here.

301
00:19:19,463 --> 00:19:21,931
I'm glad you came.

302
00:19:27,028 --> 00:19:29,530
There you go.

303
00:19:29,530 --> 00:19:33,400
I was planning to text you
to say this was my mom's treat.

304
00:19:35,169 --> 00:19:38,005
But you might not show up.

305
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:41,979
Come on. I can deal with your mom.

306
00:19:41,979 --> 00:19:43,868
There.

307
00:19:43,868 --> 00:19:46,748
Mommy, how are you?

308
00:19:46,748 --> 00:19:49,416
So you're back from Thailand.

309
00:19:50,651 --> 00:19:52,752
I made sure to come back

310
00:19:52,752 --> 00:19:55,256
to be in my grandson's moving-up ceremony.

311
00:19:55,256 --> 00:20:00,627
I just shipped
all the beauty products I bought.

312
00:20:03,631 --> 00:20:05,866
So, Liam.

313
00:20:07,468 --> 00:20:09,903
Do you still have the same job?

314
00:20:11,606 --> 00:20:15,476
Yes. I still work at the TV network.

315
00:20:15,476 --> 00:20:18,979
So, did you get promoted?

316
00:20:20,615 --> 00:20:23,918
I'm still a writer.

317
00:20:23,918 --> 00:20:29,156
There are lots of senior writers
who are ahead of me.

318
00:20:33,526 --> 00:20:37,298
I'm glad you're still in showbiz...

319
00:20:37,298 --> 00:20:39,200
Unlike Joyce,

320
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,903
who never went back to acting
after giving birth.

321
00:20:46,274 --> 00:20:48,443
Don't worry, Mommy.

322
00:20:48,443 --> 00:20:51,745
I'm taking care of my wife and my son.

323
00:20:53,114 --> 00:20:54,682
Really?

324
00:20:54,682 --> 00:20:58,119
I think it's the other way around.

325
00:20:58,119 --> 00:21:01,122
Joyce makes more money
from selling insurance.

326
00:21:01,122 --> 00:21:03,491
Mommy, please.

327
00:21:03,491 --> 00:21:04,725
Why?

328
00:21:04,725 --> 00:21:07,695
Are you going to defend your husband?

329
00:21:07,695 --> 00:21:11,498
He's the reason my dreams for you got ruined.

330
00:21:12,467 --> 00:21:16,517
Everything that has happened to us
was our choice.

331
00:21:17,738 --> 00:21:20,440
Look at where you are now.

332
00:21:21,042 --> 00:21:25,712
I don't know how to respond
to what people say about you.

333
00:21:26,543 --> 00:21:29,945
That! Your fall from stardom!

334
00:21:31,252 --> 00:21:36,657
Joyce, you know everything I've done for you,

335
00:21:36,657 --> 00:21:38,692
for your career!

336
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:41,362
But what happened?

337
00:21:41,362 --> 00:21:42,830
You ruined it!

338
00:21:42,830 --> 00:21:45,632
You both ruined it!

339
00:21:56,008 --> 00:21:57,378
Ma'am!

340
00:21:57,378 --> 00:21:58,446
Excuse me.

341
00:21:58,446 --> 00:22:02,583
Madam, aren't you a former sexy star?

342
00:22:02,583 --> 00:22:05,520
Madam! I knew it! It's you!

343
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:07,855
Madam, my mother is a big fan of yours!

344
00:22:07,855 --> 00:22:09,056
- And my father too...
- You know me?

345
00:22:09,056 --> 00:22:10,191
Yes, Madam!

346
00:22:10,191 --> 00:22:13,027
My father has a calendar
with your picture in it.

347
00:22:13,027 --> 00:22:15,530
My neighbors get rowdy
whenever you appear on TV, Madam!

348
00:22:15,530 --> 00:22:17,865
- My gosh!
- You're so beautiful!

349
00:22:17,865 --> 00:22:19,634
Oh, thank you.

350
00:22:19,634 --> 00:22:22,001
Madam, can I have a picture with you?

351
00:22:22,001 --> 00:22:23,704
Sure, sure!

352
00:22:23,704 --> 00:22:24,772
Sure.

353
00:22:24,772 --> 00:22:27,808
- There.
- You're still so fresh, Madam.

354
00:22:27,808 --> 00:22:29,110
You smell so good!

355
00:22:29,110 --> 00:22:30,945
Can I have a fan sign, too, Madam?

356
00:22:30,945 --> 00:22:32,046
I always bring this with me.

357
00:22:32,046 --> 00:22:33,581
I know I will see you someday, Madam.

358
00:22:33,581 --> 00:22:35,816
- Okay, sure.
- This is my mom and my dad.

359
00:22:35,816 --> 00:22:37,385
- Fidel and Andeng.
- Fidel and Andeng.

360
00:22:37,385 --> 00:22:40,087
- Okay.
- Okay, please smile, Madam.

361
00:22:40,087 --> 00:22:42,822
One, two...

362
00:22:42,822 --> 00:22:44,659
- Thank you, Madam.
- Thank you, thank you.

363
00:22:44,659 --> 00:22:46,327
Sorry for getting so excited.

364
00:22:46,327 --> 00:22:47,595
It's okay.

365
00:22:47,595 --> 00:22:50,197
- Thank you, thank you.
- I'm at the other table...

366
00:23:12,119 --> 00:23:13,657
Mommy.

367
00:23:14,956 --> 00:23:16,990
Mommy, I'm sorry.

368
00:23:17,658 --> 00:23:19,660
I'm sorry. I know...

369
00:23:19,660 --> 00:23:21,762
I know you got hurt by everything I said.

370
00:23:21,762 --> 00:23:24,064
I didn't mean it.

371
00:23:26,434 --> 00:23:30,938
I don't care about what you said.

372
00:23:30,938 --> 00:23:36,555
What I'm concerned about is that
you were caught on video, drinking!

373
00:23:36,555 --> 00:23:39,891
You know you can't be seen drinking
because of your endorsements!

374
00:23:43,851 --> 00:23:45,919
Really, Mommy?

375
00:23:47,855 --> 00:23:50,791
Is that all you care about? Endorsements?

376
00:23:50,791 --> 00:23:52,559
Yes!

377
00:23:53,294 --> 00:23:56,096
- Money?
- Of course!

378
00:23:59,533 --> 00:24:04,672
Don't you think
we should talk about the real issue?

379
00:24:04,672 --> 00:24:10,511
Can't you see or feel
that I need even just a little space, Mom?

380
00:24:10,511 --> 00:24:12,612
Just a little space!

381
00:24:14,155 --> 00:24:15,816
Wow.

382
00:24:15,816 --> 00:24:21,368
And you want to have control
over your life and career?

383
00:24:21,368 --> 00:24:22,857
To be ordinary?

384
00:24:22,857 --> 00:24:25,660
To drink every night? Get wasted every night?

385
00:24:25,660 --> 00:24:27,727
Is that the life you want?

386
00:24:29,330 --> 00:24:31,532
How about your image?

387
00:24:31,532 --> 00:24:33,901
Do you want to be ordinary?

388
00:24:33,901 --> 00:24:35,836
Go ahead!

389
00:24:35,836 --> 00:24:40,073
If I had let you decide for yourself,

390
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:45,175
you would have probably
lost your career already.

391
00:24:45,998 --> 00:24:47,623
You...

392
00:24:48,854 --> 00:24:52,107
would have gotten pregnant.

393
00:24:52,107 --> 00:24:55,389
There goes your career, just like that.

394
00:24:55,389 --> 00:24:57,357
You're on your own now.

395
00:25:17,267 --> 00:25:20,214
Maxine, you guys were
the only ones with me that night.

396
00:25:20,214 --> 00:25:22,083
I think I saw you taking a video of me.

397
00:25:22,083 --> 00:25:24,253
Who leaked the video?

398
00:25:24,253 --> 00:25:26,187
Hey, Savana!

399
00:25:26,187 --> 00:25:29,824
Don't you know that's slander?

400
00:25:29,824 --> 00:25:32,467
That's why I'm asking you.

401
00:25:32,467 --> 00:25:35,501
<i>I don't know who did it. I already told you.</i>

402
00:25:35,501 --> 00:25:37,866
<i>I don't know who's the girl with...</i>

403
00:25:37,866 --> 00:25:42,570
whatsoever hair
who uploaded your video, okay?

404
00:25:42,570 --> 00:25:45,707
And why don't you look for her?

405
00:25:45,707 --> 00:25:49,010
I want to know where the video came from!

406
00:25:49,010 --> 00:25:50,912
<i>I have no idea!</i>

407
00:25:50,912 --> 00:25:55,634
You were so drunk that night, Savana.

408
00:25:55,634 --> 00:25:56,701
You didn't notice

409
00:25:56,701 --> 00:26:00,355
that a lot of people were taking
a video of you.

410
00:26:00,355 --> 00:26:03,910
So, please.

411
00:26:03,911 --> 00:26:06,611
Don't drag me into your problem.

412
00:26:21,901 --> 00:26:23,378
Savana.

413
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:31,809
She's a coward
for hiding in an alter identity.

414
00:26:31,810 --> 00:26:33,896
Don't worry.

415
00:26:36,593 --> 00:26:39,128
Hans, why are you here?

416
00:26:40,297 --> 00:26:43,767
Did you cut short your trip to Mindanao
just to be here?

417
00:26:43,767 --> 00:26:47,320
I know you have important things
that you need to attend to.

418
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:48,099
Savana...

419
00:26:48,100 --> 00:26:51,139
The victims of land grabbing need you,
but you're here.

420
00:26:51,139 --> 00:26:56,029
Savana, I've completed the initial work
in Mindanao.

421
00:26:56,029 --> 00:26:57,767
And I was there as a human rights lawyer

422
00:26:57,767 --> 00:27:02,099
to help the oppressed and powerless.

423
00:27:02,100 --> 00:27:05,332
Like how you are in trouble
because of that online predator.

424
00:27:05,333 --> 00:27:06,926
Don't worry.

425
00:27:06,927 --> 00:27:09,562
I'm here to protect you.

426
00:27:11,161 --> 00:27:15,606
But in every case you handle,
you know who's the victim.

427
00:27:16,570 --> 00:27:19,503
But my problem is...

428
00:27:19,503 --> 00:27:22,500
I know someone from the NBI.

429
00:27:22,501 --> 00:27:24,708
I talked to him already.

430
00:27:24,708 --> 00:27:28,577
He will help us find
that online streaming channel.

431
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:34,362
Thank you, Hans.

432
00:27:34,363 --> 00:27:36,531
Thank you for being here.

433
00:27:38,121 --> 00:27:40,696
I'm always here for you, Savana.

434
00:27:40,697 --> 00:27:43,499
I promise we'll find a way to resolve this.

435
00:27:58,639 --> 00:28:04,766
Everyone, I would like
to introduce Attorney Hans Arevalo.

436
00:28:04,767 --> 00:28:07,048
Good afternoon. Nice to meet you.

437
00:28:09,081 --> 00:28:11,850
He's a lawyer.

438
00:28:11,851 --> 00:28:13,879
Perfect!

439
00:28:13,879 --> 00:28:15,020
Hey.

440
00:28:15,020 --> 00:28:17,012
Is he your boyfriend, Savana?

441
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:22,851
Well, I'm not ashamed to say
that I'm her suitor.

442
00:28:26,754 --> 00:28:28,022
Hello, good afternoon.

443
00:28:28,022 --> 00:28:29,190
- I'm Hans.
- Via.

444
00:28:29,190 --> 00:28:30,624
Nice to meet you, Via.

445
00:28:30,624 --> 00:28:32,096
Hans.

446
00:28:33,828 --> 00:28:35,291
Liam.

447
00:28:37,298 --> 00:28:38,966
So, Liam.

448
00:28:38,966 --> 00:28:45,773
Are you the head of the creative team
that develops Savana's movie?

449
00:28:45,773 --> 00:28:47,676
Yeah, creative manager.

450
00:28:47,676 --> 00:28:49,810
Oh, that's nice.

451
00:28:49,810 --> 00:28:54,782
I'm glad you're with Savana right now.

452
00:28:54,782 --> 00:28:57,885
At least you know what she's going through.

453
00:28:57,885 --> 00:29:01,455
Since you're in the same industry.

454
00:29:01,455 --> 00:29:05,440
I'll do my best to find out
who uploaded the video.

455
00:29:06,894 --> 00:29:09,646
That's what I promised Savana, too.

456
00:29:11,332 --> 00:29:13,467
Hi, Hans.

457
00:29:13,467 --> 00:29:15,503
Please help Savana.

458
00:29:15,503 --> 00:29:19,707
You know a lot of people
in the Cybercrime Division.

459
00:29:19,707 --> 00:29:22,181
Of course, Auntie. You can count on me.

460
00:29:23,344 --> 00:29:25,101
Thank you for being so reliable.

461
00:29:25,101 --> 00:29:28,279
And I can't wait for you
to become my son-in-law.

462
00:29:31,852 --> 00:29:34,855
Anyway, we have to go.

463
00:29:34,855 --> 00:29:38,381
I still have to clean up a lot of mess.

464
00:29:48,836 --> 00:29:50,504
Okay, that's our last baggage.

465
00:29:50,504 --> 00:29:53,374
Please bring it to the car.

466
00:29:53,374 --> 00:29:55,376
Auntie, I'll convoy your car.

467
00:29:55,376 --> 00:29:56,981
Okay.

468
00:30:02,449 --> 00:30:05,369
Sir, are you going to join us
in the service vehicle?

469
00:30:09,390 --> 00:30:11,025
It's up to you, Love.

470
00:30:11,025 --> 00:30:12,259
It's fine by me.

471
00:30:12,259 --> 00:30:14,762
Whatever you want.

472
00:30:14,762 --> 00:30:17,228
It's okay with me to drive.

473
00:30:20,434 --> 00:30:23,070
No, I'll go with Via.

474
00:30:23,070 --> 00:30:24,438
We'll go ahead, then.

475
00:30:24,438 --> 00:30:26,014
- We'll go ahead.
- Be safe.

476
00:30:26,014 --> 00:30:27,217
Bye.

477
00:30:28,043 --> 00:30:31,286
That's mine. Thank you.

478
00:30:32,207 --> 00:30:34,431
Boss Bro.

479
00:30:34,431 --> 00:30:36,650
I'll ride with them.

480
00:30:37,912 --> 00:30:41,381
Looks like you and Ma'am Via
still have a lot to talk about.

481
00:30:46,093 --> 00:30:47,795
- Bye, Ma'am Via.
- Be safe.

482
00:30:47,795 --> 00:30:48,996
Let's go together, Borj.

483
00:30:48,996 --> 00:30:50,798
- Why?
- Let's go.

484
00:30:50,798 --> 00:30:53,066
- I can go by myself.
- Let's go.

485
00:30:56,103 --> 00:30:57,587
Let me have that.

486
00:30:58,697 --> 00:31:00,330
Love.

487
00:31:02,103 --> 00:31:03,869
About last night...

488
00:31:04,959 --> 00:31:07,114
I'm sorry.

489
00:31:07,114 --> 00:31:09,149
I got so drunk.

490
00:31:09,149 --> 00:31:11,486
Did I say something inappropriate?

491
00:31:13,740 --> 00:31:14,589
Love.

492
00:31:14,590 --> 00:31:16,626
Joyce...

493
00:31:17,438 --> 00:31:19,337
Joyce.

494
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:25,306
Never mind.

495
00:31:26,300 --> 00:31:29,290
As you said, you were drunk.

496
00:31:30,170 --> 00:31:31,720
Let's go home.

497
00:31:50,691 --> 00:31:54,828
Are you keeping an eye
on Tristan and Savana's film?

498
00:31:54,828 --> 00:31:59,066
The campaign period will begin
in a couple of months.

499
00:31:59,066 --> 00:32:03,518
We need to make sure
that my godson's popularity will rise.

500
00:32:04,620 --> 00:32:06,874
Don't worry, Uncle Ramon.

501
00:32:06,874 --> 00:32:09,476
It's a tried and tested formula.

502
00:32:09,476 --> 00:32:14,466
Your movies become blockbuster hits
before the campaign period.

503
00:32:14,466 --> 00:32:18,519
I'm sure it will also work for Tristan.

504
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:21,524
The movie will help him win the elections.

505
00:32:22,356 --> 00:32:26,374
But looks like we have a problem with Savana.

506
00:32:35,953 --> 00:32:37,204
<i>Cry.</i>

507
00:32:37,204 --> 00:32:40,941
<i>Savana, you should shed tears
only through your left eye.</i>

508
00:32:40,941 --> 00:32:43,711
<i>Savana... Savana, don't eat that!</i>

509
00:32:43,711 --> 00:32:46,700
<i>Savana, you look so fat.</i>

510
00:33:13,877 --> 00:33:17,113
Are you going to sacrifice your queen, Uncle?

511
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:29,526
Check.

512
00:33:42,770 --> 00:33:44,417
Checkmate.

513
00:33:49,109 --> 00:33:51,042
Now you know.

514
00:33:51,945 --> 00:33:57,002
There's something you need to sacrifice
to win.

515
00:34:11,832 --> 00:34:14,468
<i>I don't care who suffers, Liam.</i>

516
00:34:14,468 --> 00:34:18,682
<i>I won't let you become the hero
in dad's eyes again.</i>

517
00:34:20,729 --> 00:34:22,214
Uncle.

518
00:34:27,648 --> 00:34:29,479
One more game?

519
00:34:32,152 --> 00:34:34,401
You got me there, Uncle.

520
00:34:47,034 --> 00:34:48,969
What kind of juice is this?

521
00:34:48,969 --> 00:34:50,137
Is this fresh?

522
00:34:50,137 --> 00:34:51,538
Of course!

523
00:34:51,538 --> 00:34:53,740
It's so fresh, just like you.

524
00:34:53,740 --> 00:34:55,418
I like it even if there's no ice in it.

525
00:34:55,418 --> 00:34:58,421
But it needs more sugar.

526
00:34:58,422 --> 00:34:59,087
There's no ice

527
00:34:59,088 --> 00:35:01,412
because we don't want you
to have a sore throat.

528
00:35:01,412 --> 00:35:02,983
There's still a concert coming up.

529
00:35:02,983 --> 00:35:04,918
But put more sugar next time, okay?

530
00:35:04,918 --> 00:35:06,320
Noted, Madam!

531
00:35:06,320 --> 00:35:09,723
I will make it sweeter for you next time.

532
00:35:09,723 --> 00:35:11,058
True!

533
00:35:11,058 --> 00:35:13,263
- Thank you.
- Of course, Madam. Anytime.

534
00:35:13,263 --> 00:35:16,282
Okay, thank you. Bye!

535
00:35:19,766 --> 00:35:22,643
Good evening.

536
00:35:22,643 --> 00:35:25,606
Madam, we're ready.

537
00:35:25,606 --> 00:35:26,940
Are you ready?

538
00:35:26,940 --> 00:35:28,842
We're ready, too. Let's begin. Let's go.

539
00:35:28,842 --> 00:35:31,811
- Let's do this.
- Yes.

540
00:35:32,513 --> 00:35:36,250
Mom, why do we have to do this?

541
00:35:36,250 --> 00:35:40,212
Didn't I say that I would clean up your mess?

542
00:35:42,890 --> 00:35:44,292
- Let's go.
- Yes.

543
00:35:44,292 --> 00:35:45,460
- Let's do this.
- Come on.

544
00:35:45,460 --> 00:35:47,620
Okay.

545
00:35:50,731 --> 00:35:53,601
A manager and a mother...

546
00:35:53,601 --> 00:35:58,439
Those are the roles I play
in my daughter's life.

547
00:35:58,439 --> 00:36:00,575
It is not easy.

548
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:04,412
There's only one thing on my mind.

549
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:07,021
My daughter's welfare.

550
00:36:08,882 --> 00:36:13,988
I admit
that I am sometimes strict with Savana.

551
00:36:13,988 --> 00:36:18,893
But it's normal for every parent, right?

552
00:36:18,893 --> 00:36:24,098
And it's normal
for people her age to party...

553
00:36:24,098 --> 00:36:27,454
- To have fun, right?
- True.

554
00:36:28,803 --> 00:36:35,750
Those malicious videos of Savana
that came out...

555
00:36:36,511 --> 00:36:41,983
People don't know that those were edited.

556
00:36:41,983 --> 00:36:43,752
- Edited?
- Yes.

557
00:36:43,752 --> 00:36:46,287
- Oh my God, edited.
- Spliced.

558
00:36:46,287 --> 00:36:47,855
My God.

559
00:36:47,855 --> 00:36:52,426
People will do everything
to bring others down.

560
00:36:52,426 --> 00:36:54,929
I know.

561
00:36:54,929 --> 00:37:02,920
They only showed the part
where Savana was venting out.

562
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:05,773
They didn't show the whole context.

563
00:37:05,773 --> 00:37:07,642
The whole video.

564
00:37:07,642 --> 00:37:09,677
I see.

565
00:37:09,677 --> 00:37:13,159
So after everything,

566
00:37:13,159 --> 00:37:17,718
Savana told me that she understands
where I was coming from,

567
00:37:17,718 --> 00:37:24,679
being her manager and her mother.

568
00:37:25,626 --> 00:37:28,054
She assured me...

569
00:37:29,730 --> 00:37:34,702
that our relationship wouldn't change...

570
00:37:34,702 --> 00:37:38,339
That she wouldn't change a thing.

571
00:37:38,339 --> 00:37:40,341
Savana, dear.

572
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:42,710
Sweetie, come here.

573
00:37:42,710 --> 00:37:46,546
Come here, dear. Sit beside your mom.

574
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:55,243
Go and sit by her side.

575
00:38:12,505 --> 00:38:16,430
To those who watched my video...

576
00:38:21,215 --> 00:38:22,821
It's true.

577
00:38:24,352 --> 00:38:27,302
It was edited.

578
00:38:30,625 --> 00:38:35,435
That's not what really happened.

579
00:38:37,898 --> 00:38:41,162
I apologize to everyone.

580
00:38:41,162 --> 00:38:42,912
I'm sorry...

581
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:49,966
Especially to you, Mommy.

582
00:38:52,480 --> 00:38:55,650
I'm sorry. I love you so much.

583
00:38:55,650 --> 00:38:56,917
I know that, Sweetie.

584
00:38:56,917 --> 00:38:59,052
I know that.

585
00:39:18,272 --> 00:39:20,775
Love, is something bothering you?

586
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:23,710
You've been checking your phone
since earlier.

587
00:39:25,112 --> 00:39:28,082
Vergil keeps sending me messages.

588
00:39:28,082 --> 00:39:32,027
He's calling for an emergency meeting
tomorrow at Blacksmith.

589
00:39:32,027 --> 00:39:34,870
He won't say what it's for.

590
00:39:45,528 --> 00:39:48,057
I want a cake.

591
00:39:50,171 --> 00:39:52,502
Can you buy it for me, Love?

592
00:39:54,642 --> 00:39:56,689
Yeah, sure.

593
00:40:14,834 --> 00:40:18,132
[Contacts: Joyce]

594
00:40:18,133 --> 00:40:20,401
[No results for "Joyce"]

595
00:40:20,401 --> 00:40:22,227
Joyce?

596
00:40:24,938 --> 00:40:27,347
Joycelyn Trinidad.

597
00:40:34,213 --> 00:40:36,515
Who is this?

598
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:46,593
Who is this?

599
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:12,473
Thank you.

600
00:41:12,473 --> 00:41:13,738
Yeah.

601
00:41:25,901 --> 00:41:27,474
Via, I'm sorry.

602
00:41:27,474 --> 00:41:29,970
Can we go home?

603
00:41:29,970 --> 00:41:34,728
I still need to inform the team
about our emergency meeting.

604
00:41:37,004 --> 00:41:39,103
You can call them now.

605
00:41:42,908 --> 00:41:44,551
It's okay.

606
00:41:46,861 --> 00:41:49,657
I still need to pack my things.

607
00:41:49,657 --> 00:41:52,283
So I really need to go home.

608
00:42:02,402 --> 00:42:04,237
I'll finish this cake first.

609
00:42:04,237 --> 00:42:06,239
- Sure.
- Okay.

610
00:42:06,239 --> 00:42:07,774
Do you want to try it?

611
00:42:07,774 --> 00:42:09,072
No.

612
00:42:13,947 --> 00:42:16,510
Good luck with your meeting tomorrow.

613
00:42:18,251 --> 00:42:19,740
Thank you.

614
00:42:26,654 --> 00:42:31,164
Arnel, the action scenes in this movie

615
00:42:31,164 --> 00:42:33,099
should be more challenging
than what we did before.

616
00:42:33,099 --> 00:42:35,068
- Okay?
- Okay. Go, Arnel.

617
00:42:35,068 --> 00:42:36,803
- Show them what you got.
- Okay, go.

618
00:42:36,803 --> 00:42:37,804
Show them, Arnel.

619
00:42:37,804 --> 00:42:39,272
- Show them!
- Go, Arnel!

620
00:42:39,272 --> 00:42:40,440
Go, Arnel!

621
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:42,075
There you go!

622
00:42:46,161 --> 00:42:47,313
Oh my! Arnel.

623
00:42:47,313 --> 00:42:49,033
- Go check on him, Megan.
- Arnel. What have you done, Torong?

624
00:42:49,033 --> 00:42:52,167
- Arnel...
- Arnel, are you still alive?

625
00:42:52,167 --> 00:42:53,820
- My God.
- Oh, my!

626
00:42:53,820 --> 00:42:55,942
What? Is he okay?

627
00:42:55,942 --> 00:42:59,325
He's still alive.
What were you doing, Torong?

628
00:42:59,325 --> 00:43:01,273
- Hey.
- Arnel.

629
00:43:01,273 --> 00:43:03,429
- You overdid it.
- Arnel.

630
00:43:03,429 --> 00:43:05,601
Arnel.

631
00:43:05,601 --> 00:43:08,034
- Get up.
- Can you get up?

632
00:43:08,034 --> 00:43:10,100
Sir, what is this audition for?

633
00:43:10,100 --> 00:43:12,105
A movie or a wrestling team?

634
00:43:12,105 --> 00:43:14,307
Come on, Arnel.

635
00:43:14,307 --> 00:43:16,009
You've become rusty.

636
00:43:16,009 --> 00:43:18,811
You used to be my best stuntman.

637
00:43:18,811 --> 00:43:21,514
The movie has great vision.

638
00:43:21,514 --> 00:43:23,316
This is action.

639
00:43:23,316 --> 00:43:24,617
Okay?

640
00:43:24,617 --> 00:43:28,087
But you know, this is not lovely for me.

641
00:43:28,087 --> 00:43:29,055
Sorry, Director.

642
00:43:29,055 --> 00:43:30,690
- Let's try it again.
- Okay.

643
00:43:30,690 --> 00:43:33,660
- One more time.
- Come on, let's do it again.

644
00:43:33,660 --> 00:43:34,794
Torong, be careful.

645
00:43:34,794 --> 00:43:36,929
I don't want to bring anyone to the hospital.

646
00:43:36,929 --> 00:43:39,699
- Be careful, Torong.
- Come on, Torong.

647
00:43:39,699 --> 00:43:41,765
Go!

648
00:43:41,765 --> 00:43:43,503
Arnel.

649
00:43:43,503 --> 00:43:45,171
Arnel!

650
00:43:45,171 --> 00:43:47,617
What the? Arnel!

651
00:43:47,617 --> 00:43:48,868
Gosh.

652
00:43:48,868 --> 00:43:51,594
Arnel, you should rest first.

653
00:43:51,594 --> 00:43:53,046
Let's see the others.

654
00:43:53,046 --> 00:43:54,881
- Okay, rest, Arnel.
- Okay, let's see the others.

655
00:43:54,881 --> 00:43:55,923
Next one.

656
00:43:55,923 --> 00:43:57,250
Next.

657
00:43:57,250 --> 00:43:59,553
Torong, be careful.

658
00:43:59,553 --> 00:44:03,085
Torong, Torong. Torong, be careful.

659
00:44:04,057 --> 00:44:05,025
Torong.

660
00:44:05,025 --> 00:44:07,260
- He beat everyone up.
- This is nuts.

661
00:44:07,260 --> 00:44:08,335
Three, five...

662
00:44:08,335 --> 00:44:09,930
Three, five, seven.

663
00:44:09,930 --> 00:44:11,264
- Ask them to come back, okay?
- Okay.

664
00:44:11,264 --> 00:44:12,890
Hi, Director.

665
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:14,801
- Sir.
- Hello, Sir.

666
00:44:14,801 --> 00:44:16,136
- Hello, Sir.
- Hi, Sir.

667
00:44:16,136 --> 00:44:18,077
Hello, Sir.

668
00:44:20,507 --> 00:44:22,038
What do you have here?

669
00:44:22,038 --> 00:44:23,276
We have an audition.

670
00:44:23,276 --> 00:44:25,626
We have chosen
one of the action scenes already.

671
00:44:25,626 --> 00:44:28,682
- It's getting less and less.
- Action teams.

672
00:44:28,682 --> 00:44:30,517
From 100, here it is now.

673
00:44:30,517 --> 00:44:31,852
This looks okay.

674
00:44:31,852 --> 00:44:33,020
That one.

675
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:34,354
- Number three...
- His built looks good.

676
00:44:34,354 --> 00:44:37,024
He's good with dialogue.

677
00:44:37,024 --> 00:44:38,325
- This one?
- Yes.

678
00:44:38,325 --> 00:44:39,693
This one is good.

679
00:44:39,693 --> 00:44:41,828
That one is okay, Sir.

680
00:44:41,828 --> 00:44:44,765
- Ask this one for a callback, too.
- Okay, I will.

681
00:44:46,168 --> 00:44:48,136
- Next!
- Boss Bro...

682
00:44:50,976 --> 00:44:52,907
Savana, Auntie.

683
00:44:52,907 --> 00:44:54,809
Hello.

684
00:44:54,809 --> 00:44:57,548
What is the agenda for today's meeting?

685
00:44:58,813 --> 00:45:02,282
I've yet to find out for myself.

686
00:45:13,995 --> 00:45:16,164
Good morning, everyone.

687
00:45:16,164 --> 00:45:18,166
It's nice to meet all of you.

688
00:45:18,166 --> 00:45:20,669
I can't wait to win this election.

689
00:45:20,669 --> 00:45:24,339
I want to introduce to all of you
my new protégé.

690
00:45:24,339 --> 00:45:28,143
My other godson, Josh.

691
00:45:28,143 --> 00:45:31,012
Okay, let's win this election.

692
00:45:31,012 --> 00:45:35,016
With Josh, you are the boss.

693
00:45:48,697 --> 00:45:51,366
What are these clothes
that you got from Dmitri?

694
00:45:51,366 --> 00:45:53,487
Did you choose these?

695
00:45:54,690 --> 00:45:56,638
My God!

696
00:45:56,638 --> 00:45:59,341
I know drag queens
who have better taste than this.

697
00:45:59,341 --> 00:46:00,875
Have you shown these to Miss Via?

698
00:46:00,875 --> 00:46:03,242
We've already sent her pictures.

699
00:46:03,242 --> 00:46:04,579
There it is.

700
00:46:04,579 --> 00:46:06,214
She sent me a message already.

701
00:46:06,214 --> 00:46:09,016
You explain this to our boss.

702
00:46:11,190 --> 00:46:19,060
"I want you to research a woman
named Joycelyn Trinidad."

703
00:46:19,060 --> 00:46:21,334
Joycelyn Trinidad.

704
00:46:22,568 --> 00:46:24,959
What did Miss Via say?

705
00:46:25,935 --> 00:46:27,269
Not work related.

706
00:46:27,269 --> 00:46:29,685
Go back to your work.

707
00:46:29,685 --> 00:46:31,107
Go!

708
00:46:33,108 --> 00:46:38,842
Hello, Miss. What's the tea about this woman?

709
00:46:54,229 --> 00:46:57,132
About your other godson.

710
00:46:57,132 --> 00:46:59,967
Is he sure about his identity?

711
00:47:01,702 --> 00:47:04,204
I'm going to give this round
to you and your daughter.

712
00:47:04,204 --> 00:47:06,673
Are you really serious about this?

713
00:47:06,673 --> 00:47:08,142
Of course, Uncle.

714
00:47:08,142 --> 00:47:11,612
This is the chance my father gave me
to prove myself.

715
00:47:11,612 --> 00:47:13,580
I don't think you understand.

716
00:47:13,580 --> 00:47:20,420
I want Josh to win the elections
through this film.

717
00:47:25,160 --> 00:47:26,650
Hey!

718
00:47:29,583 --> 00:47:31,361
Are you okay?

719
00:47:33,534 --> 00:47:36,637
Oh, Liam. Have you really gone insane?

720
00:47:36,637 --> 00:47:39,540
You can go against everyone
except Congressman Ramon.

721
00:47:39,540 --> 00:47:41,575
If not, you'll get what you deserve.

722
00:47:41,575 --> 00:47:43,877
I've found Joycelyn Trinidad,

723
00:47:43,877 --> 00:47:46,045
the woman you told me to look for.
